706
00:55:44.755 --> 00:55:49.465
another and potentially more impactful benefit of parallel computing for big data.

707
00:55:49.465 --> 00:55:53.831
Instead of needing to load all of the data in one computer's memory, you can

708
00:55:53.831 --> 00:55:58.140
partition the data and load the subsets into memory of different computers.

709
00:55:58.140 --> 00:56:02.902
That means the memory footprint per computer is relatively small, and the data can

710
00:56:02.902 --> 00:56:07.723
fit in the memory closest to the processor, the RAM. Before you start rewriting all

711
