4619
06:11:30.560 --> 06:11:35.466
A basic if statement has the following structure. You start by setting up the

4620
06:11:35.466 --> 06:11:40.754
condition with the word if, followed by, in square brackets, the condition. Next is

4621
06:11:40.754 --> 06:11:46.042
a semicolon, then the word then. You then add your code to execute if the condition

4622
06:11:46.042 --> 06:11:51.394
is true. Optionally, you can have an else statement, which executes if the condition

4623
06:11:51.394 --> 06:11:56.363
specified is not true. You finish with the word fi, which is if backwards. Two

4624
06:11:56.363 --> 06:11:59.230
