6735
08:43:58.100 --> 08:44:03.159
As we get more tasks to execute, we want our tool to work with multiple machines,

6736
08:44:03.159 --> 08:44:08.280
rather than increasing the performance of one single machine. Airflow fulfills all

6737
08:44:08.280 --> 08:44:13.526
of these needs, which is why it is a good replacement for Cron. The central piece in

6738
08:44:13.526 --> 08:44:18.585
an Airflow workflow is the DAG, which is an acronym for Directed Acyclic Graph. A

6739
08:44:18.585 --> 08:44:22.270
graph is a collection of nodes that are connected by edges.

6740
08:44:22.270 --> 08:44:27.492
The directed part in the acronym implies that there is a sense of direction between

6741
08:44:27.492 --> 08:44:32.652
the nodes. The arrows on the edges indicate the direction. The acyclic part simply

6742
08:44:32.652 --> 08:44:37.811
means that when you traverse the directed graph, there is no way for you to circle

6743
