10051
13:10:49.916 --> 13:10:54.511
everything that implies here, but understand that Spark is designed to use immutable

10052
13:10:54.511 --> 13:10:58.833
objects. Practically, this means Spark data frames are defined once and are not

10053
13:10:58.833 --> 13:11:03.319
modifiable after initialization. If the variable name is reused, the original data

10054
13:11:03.319 --> 13:11:05.890
is removed, assuming it's not in use elsewhere.

10055
13:11:05.890 --> 13:11:10.367
And the variable name is reassigned to the new data. While this seems inefficient,

10056
13:11:10.367 --> 13:11:14.899
it actually allows Spark to share data between all cluster components. It can do so

10057
13:11:14.899 --> 13:11:18.994
without worry about concurrent data objects. This is a quick example of the

10058
13:11:18.994 --> 13:11:23.471
