10905
14:14:53.719 --> 14:14:58.750
Simply provide a means to disable log statements that trigger an action. A better

10906
14:14:58.750 --> 14:15:03.780
solution may exist, but this one serves to illustrate the key idea. Namely, allow

10907
14:15:03.780 --> 14:15:08.500
for data frame actions that you need during development or during debugging.

10908
14:15:08.500 --> 14:15:14.113
Yet want to disable in production while doing so with confidence that they will not

10909
14:15:14.113 --> 14:15:19.591
be silently executed setting enabled equals true here allows us to enable the log

10910
14:15:19.591 --> 14:15:25.204
statement the takeaway here is to remember that actions on large data frames can be

10911
14:15:25.204 --> 14:15:30.546
costly to calculate we need to be careful about including Spark operations that

10912
14:15:30.546 --> 14:15:33.860
trigger an action in log statement let's practice

