16:09:18.268 --> 16:09:24.024
triggers after completing this course you will feel confident implementing and using

12257
16:09:24.024 --> 16:09:29.644
triggers in your day-to-day tasks let's get started a trigger is a special type of

12258
16:09:29.644 --> 16:09:30.740
stored procedure

12259
16:09:30.740 --> 16:09:37.286
that is automatically executed when events like data modifications occur on the

12260
16:09:37.286 --> 16:09:44.080
database server. In terms of Transact SQL, TSQL commands, there are three types of

12261
16:09:44.080 --> 16:09:50.543
triggers in SQL Server. Data Manipulation Language are executed when a user or

12262
16:09:50.543 --> 16:09:56.260
process modifies data through an insert, update, or delete statement.

12263
16:09:56.260 --> 16:10:02.226
