12376
16:19:27.867 --> 16:19:33.048
created. Let's break down the list of database objects and events involved when

12377
16:19:33.048 --> 16:19:38.558
working with triggers. To make use of an insert, update or delete statement, we need

12378
16:19:38.558 --> 16:19:43.936
to have a table or view to work with. Remember the fact that a trigger needs to be

12379
16:19:43.936 --> 16:19:49.445
attached to a database object. This means a table is needed for the trigger creation

12380
16:19:49.445 --> 16:19:49.970
process.

12381
16:19:49.970 --> 16:19:55.268
We will use the products table for this example. Here is a preview of its columns

12382
16:19:55.268 --> 16:20:00.761
and contents. Once you have a table defined for the scope of the trigger, you should

12383
16:20:00.761 --> 16:20:05.994
